{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Upon his staff.</b> Upon his health and strength (Mekhilta)." "<b>And the striker is cleared.</b> Now would you suppose that this one who did not kill would be executed? Rather, Scripture teaches you here that they keep him confined until it is seen whether this one recovers; and so its meaning is: when this one gets up and walks on his staff — then the striker is cleared; but so long as this one has not gotten up, the striker is not cleared (Ketuvot 33)." "<b>Only his rest.</b> The loss of his work due to the illness. If he cut off his hand or his foot, we assess the loss of his work due to the illness as though he were a cucumber-watchman — for behold, even after the illness he is not fit for hand or foot work, and he has already paid him for the damage the value of his hand and his foot, as it is said: ״יָד תַּחַת יָד רֶגֶל תַּחַת רָגֶל״." "<b>And shall heal, he shall heal.</b> As the Targum renders — he shall pay the physician's fee."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {2 "קִשּׁוּאִין — cucumbers; שׁוֹמֵר קִשּׁוּאִין, 'watchman of cucumbers,' designates a worker fit only for the lightest task."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:38.816678718Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}